---
// On-demand, not static — see accessibility.astro's identical comment;
// this page is protected by the researcher account gate.
export const prerender = false;

import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Return and Refund Policy"
  description="Cloud Peptides return and refund policy."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>Order requests, not accepted orders</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting an order through our cart is a <strong>request</strong>, not an accepted order or a
    completed purchase — see our <a href="/shop-terms">Shop Terms</a>. This policy describes what
    happens to an order <strong>after</strong> it has been reviewed and accepted; it does not apply to
    a request that was never accepted.
  </p>

  <h2>All sales are final</h2>
  <p>
    All sales are final. We do not offer voluntary returns, exchanges, or refunds, except where
    required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>The one voluntary exception: customs replacement</h2>
  <p>
    The only voluntary replacement guarantee we offer is the customs replacement guarantee described
    in our <a href="/shipping">Shipping Policy</a>: if verifiable tracking or official documentation
    shows customs refused or returned your original package, we provide one replacement shipment per
    order, at no additional product or shipping charge. It is a replacement, not a cash refund, and
    it applies only when reshipping is lawful.
  </p>

  <h2>This policy does not override your legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in this policy overrides any mandatory consumer protection or refund right you have
    under the law that applies to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question about an order in the meantime, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we'll
    help directly.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
